1
00:00:00,520 --> 00:00:05,940
One dream, one wish If you want it,

2
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:08,240
gotta go over the top!

3
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,680
Setting sail and heading for the unknown.

4
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:33,380
Cutting through the
winds and waves as I go.

5
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:36,437
Gotta keep it up, never stopping, no.

6
00:00:36,520 --> 00:00:38,837
Cause I'm aiming to get there first, yeah.

7
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:41,417
It's all or nothing, no time to worry.

8
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:44,180
Do it later, right now I'm living free.

9
00:00:47,460 --> 00:00:51,477
When your foes look like
they will overwhelm you.

10
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:56,460
It means your heart's saying
this is what you can't do.

11
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:59,557
Despite all that to run is not an option.

12
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:01,657
Once they're closed, I
feel the satisfaction.

13
00:01:01,740 --> 00:01:03,937
You think I'm rude,
here's my appreciation.

14
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:07,040
When things are getting
tough, just gotta smile.

15
00:01:09,880 --> 00:01:12,317
If you are going on your way.

16
00:01:12,400 --> 00:01:14,577
And you're looking for
a fresh, brand new day.

17
00:01:14,660 --> 00:01:17,737
Then make sure your only
thought you have is.

18
00:01:17,820 --> 00:01:19,300
Yes, I can.

19
00:01:19,940 --> 00:01:22,077
As you're on your way.

20
00:01:22,160 --> 00:01:24,337
Mark maps will be made.

21
00:01:24,420 --> 00:01:27,177
Yes, with every step that you will take.

22
00:01:27,260 --> 00:01:30,397
Just look at all you've been through.

23
00:01:30,480 --> 00:01:32,137
Look ahead at new horizons.

24
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:33,997
In view shining brightly.

25
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:36,880
Oh, who knows what's waiting for you.

26
00:01:37,780 --> 00:01:40,117
Dream living, that's the way.

27
00:01:40,200 --> 00:01:42,137
Make like a hurricane.

28
00:01:42,220 --> 00:01:45,140
Now, got to make your mark today.

29
00:01:48,060 --> 00:01:50,997
One dream, one wish.

30
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:52,997
Your dreams don't run away.

31
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:55,977
Go for the knockout.

32
00:01:56,060 --> 00:01:57,980
Over the top!

33
00:02:02,340 --> 00:02:04,120
That lion dog's a giant!

34
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:05,720
Is it a pet?

35
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:08,280
This is a waste of time.

36
00:02:08,620 --> 00:02:10,032
Shouldn't we ask around?

37
00:02:10,260 --> 00:02:12,217
It wouldn't matter even if we did.

38
00:02:12,300 --> 00:02:13,660
They won't answer us.

39
00:02:14,180 --> 00:02:17,709
The people here are all under
the Shogun Orochi's influence.

40
00:02:19,220 --> 00:02:20,260
You sure?

41
00:02:20,480 --> 00:02:24,715
There's lots of normal-looking people
here who don't seem like bad guys.

42
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:28,597
Some towns people have
been here a very long time

43
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:32,057
until 20 years ago this
was a vibrant castle town.

44
00:02:32,140 --> 00:02:34,597
And many of the businesses
have stayed since then,

45
00:02:34,680 --> 00:02:40,037
but as for the houses, Orochi's
subordinates seized all the ones they liked;

46
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:43,177
only the merchants who they
deemed essential could stay;

47
00:02:43,260 --> 00:02:47,637
the others were thrown from their
homes—they can never return.

48
00:02:47,720 --> 00:02:51,857
This is such a cruel place!

49
00:02:51,940 --> 00:02:53,937
Make no mistake!

50
00:02:54,020 --> 00:02:54,850
mistake

51
00:03:19,720 --> 00:03:22,180
A sumo wrestler? But why?

52
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:26,880
Hmm, must be something crazy
going on in the town square.

53
00:03:27,120 --> 00:03:29,708
Well, since a sumo
wrestler came flying out,

54
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:32,040
I'm gonna guess it's a sumo match.

55
00:03:38,300 --> 00:03:39,500
Once again!

56
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:44,360
The Yokozuna, the flower capital,
stands victorious! Here he is!

57
00:03:44,760 --> 00:03:47,040
Who remains to challenge Ulashima?

58
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:48,700
Does anyone dare?

59
00:03:57,980 --> 00:04:00,380
Still nothing but weaklings, eh?

60
00:04:08,380 --> 00:04:09,580
Another one.

61
00:04:27,300 --> 00:04:31,320
It looks like Unashima is
still hungry for new opponents,

62
00:04:31,720 --> 00:04:34,920
he has defeated 19 men already!

63
00:04:35,460 --> 00:04:40,225
As for the number of bones that have been
broken, let's check in with the doctor!

64
00:04:41,020 --> 00:04:45,397
That's 10 arm bones, 15 leg bones,

65
00:04:45,480 --> 00:04:51,217
looking like 52 ribs, four
skulls, and let's see.

66
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:58,117
Seven backbones—I think that's 88 bones
in total and four wrestlers who flew away.

67
00:04:58,200 --> 00:05:00,857
He shows no mercy;

68
00:05:00,940 --> 00:05:05,397
his strength surpasses man.

69
00:05:05,480 --> 00:05:08,277
What you see before
you is an undefeatable!

70
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:09,190
undefeatable

71
00:05:10,300 --> 00:05:14,540
Now, let's hear a round
of applause for Unashima!

72
00:05:15,880 --> 00:05:19,360
A quick note, this is a
special match to the open.

73
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:23,820
Anyone who gets best
Unashima wins 500 gold coins!

74
00:05:23,980 --> 00:05:25,568
Go back down now, you guys!

75
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:27,800
Yeah, I'll bet on you!

76
00:05:31,180 --> 00:05:33,160
That prize is gonna be ours!

77
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:35,140
We know just what to do!

78
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:37,227
Put those scandals in their place!

79
00:05:37,310 --> 00:05:38,140
Nice!

80
00:05:38,223 --> 00:05:39,510
Crack their skulls!

81
00:05:47,130 --> 00:05:49,330
Looks like a fight!

82
00:05:52,830 --> 00:05:54,490
Get ready!

83
00:05:57,310 --> 00:05:58,140
And go!

84
00:06:11,630 --> 00:06:15,590
Okiku, you accepted my
invitation after all.

85
00:06:18,050 --> 00:06:22,050
I'm glad you finally came
around and decided to marry me.

86
00:06:25,270 --> 00:06:26,490
How awkward.

87
00:06:26,950 --> 00:06:29,430
You are way too big to hide behind me.

88
00:06:30,050 --> 00:06:32,430
Well, this is certainly a surprise!

89
00:06:32,850 --> 00:06:36,430
There's a woman here who is
apparently engaged to Unashima!

90
00:06:37,770 --> 00:06:38,600
Ah!

91
00:06:38,683 --> 00:06:43,070
Loved by a Yokozuna, I'm a little
jealous, and she came here to support him!

92
00:06:43,330 --> 00:06:46,470
This is a big day for our champion!

93
00:06:48,110 --> 00:06:49,827
Do you have a special someone?

94
00:06:49,910 --> 00:06:51,170
It's not fair!

95
00:06:51,330 --> 00:06:52,950
I want to be his wife!

96
00:06:53,790 --> 00:06:55,690
For real? Never.

97
00:06:58,210 --> 00:07:01,130
He just got that idea in his big head.

98
00:07:01,570 --> 00:07:03,982
The man can be quite forward, as you saw.

99
00:07:06,690 --> 00:07:11,130
Oh, Kiku, I'll have a wrestling
match in Bekori Town today, Pei.

100
00:07:11,590 --> 00:07:15,650
I hope you'll come so I can
show you just how strong I am.

101
00:07:20,390 --> 00:07:23,610
I assure you, I will
not budge on the issue.

102
00:07:26,330 --> 00:07:27,630
Fair enough, then.

103
00:07:28,570 --> 00:07:30,130
Hey, you guys!

104
00:07:31,050 --> 00:07:33,610
We're looking for someone! Can you help?

105
00:07:34,170 --> 00:07:35,330
A little girl!

106
00:07:35,510 --> 00:07:36,570
Her name is Tama!

107
00:07:37,030 --> 00:07:39,971
Can you tell me where the
boss of this town is at?

108
00:07:40,890 --> 00:07:42,290
She should be there!

109
00:07:43,890 --> 00:07:45,150
I'm so angry!

110
00:07:45,390 --> 00:07:46,250
It's not fair!

111
00:07:46,690 --> 00:07:48,490
I'm good at her suspender!

112
00:07:49,830 --> 00:07:53,467
She looks kind of big, but I guess
that's just right for Urashima.

113
00:07:53,550 --> 00:07:54,380
No!

114
00:07:54,463 --> 00:07:55,521
I'm the only one for him!

115
00:07:56,830 --> 00:07:58,390
They're all ignoring you.

116
00:07:59,250 --> 00:08:01,147
Hurry and do me a favor, would you?

117
00:08:01,230 --> 00:08:03,970
Grab Okiku, bring her over here.

118
00:08:05,810 --> 00:08:08,307
Congrats boss, it seems
you're quite the charmer.

119
00:08:08,390 --> 00:08:11,625
Next you're gonna have to
train us in the arts of love.

120
00:08:14,170 --> 00:08:15,000
Okiku.

121
00:08:15,210 --> 00:08:16,975
Fine, we might tell ourselves.

122
00:08:17,530 --> 00:08:18,430
Let's go.

123
00:08:21,450 --> 00:08:25,367
Hey lady, Urashima told
us to get you, come on.

124
00:08:25,450 --> 00:08:27,867
We've got stuff to do, move.

125
00:08:27,950 --> 00:08:29,670
Knock him out!

126
00:08:31,570 --> 00:08:33,430
It's your deal, huh?

127
00:08:52,710 --> 00:08:53,540
What?

128
00:08:54,190 --> 00:08:56,530
That was a pretty good charge.

129
00:09:01,450 --> 00:09:04,770
But a nice slap is still my favorite.

130
00:09:06,790 --> 00:09:09,850
Lady, why are you resisting? Stop.

131
00:09:10,210 --> 00:09:11,330
Please let me go.

132
00:09:14,910 --> 00:09:16,947
You're going to cut an unarmed man?

133
00:09:17,030 --> 00:09:18,971
I don't even have any clothes on.

134
00:09:36,390 --> 00:09:37,590
Hey, Kaku!

135
00:09:49,830 --> 00:09:53,150
Uh, Throw, why didn't you stop that guy?

136
00:09:58,210 --> 00:09:59,040
Sorry.

137
00:09:59,750 --> 00:10:02,515
But I couldn't cut down
a man in his underwear.

138
00:10:03,150 --> 00:10:04,710
Just didn't feel right.

139
00:10:05,330 --> 00:10:07,170
One, two! One, two!

140
00:10:07,690 --> 00:10:11,730
Besides, I have a feeling she's
not half as helpless as she looks.

141
00:10:18,050 --> 00:10:20,250
She's too low class to even be here.

142
00:10:20,410 --> 00:10:22,767
How did she get through the
gate in the first place?

143
00:10:22,850 --> 00:10:23,890
Kick her out!

144
00:10:24,250 --> 00:10:25,830
She's got some nerve.

145
00:10:26,690 --> 00:10:29,219
I knew she was a trip
the second I saw her.

146
00:10:31,830 --> 00:10:33,950
What would you peasants know?

147
00:10:38,370 --> 00:10:41,030
I'm a member of the
warrior class, damn it.

148
00:10:41,590 --> 00:10:45,170
You commoners are nothing but
filth beneath my feet, Perk.

149
00:10:47,170 --> 00:10:50,090
Your lives are meaningless
to someone like me.

150
00:10:50,470 --> 00:10:53,330
I may spare you, or I may slay you.

151
00:10:54,450 --> 00:10:56,530
There's nothing you can do.

152
00:11:17,690 --> 00:11:18,730
So,

153
00:11:19,050 --> 00:11:25,070
Okiku, having heard that,
ignore those vermin,

154
00:11:25,270 --> 00:11:27,310
and be mine! Please!

155
00:11:27,690 --> 00:11:29,550
I won't take no for an answer!

156
00:11:35,370 --> 00:11:41,450
What I see are people just
trying to survive, not vermin.

157
00:12:12,530 --> 00:12:17,570
Ye vulgar beast, the only filth
before me is thine own heart.

158
00:12:27,630 --> 00:12:30,390
She cut off this top knot.

159
00:12:36,390 --> 00:12:37,930
Whoa, sweet!

160
00:12:39,130 --> 00:12:40,607
Nice one!

161
00:12:40,690 --> 00:12:41,987
Go Kaku!

162
00:12:42,070 --> 00:12:45,210
This is getting fun!

163
00:12:46,710 --> 00:12:49,367
The Commodore woman rejected him hard!

164
00:12:49,450 --> 00:12:52,427
His top knot has been violated!

165
00:12:52,510 --> 00:12:55,710
The boss should be coming
for us any time now?

166
00:13:11,370 --> 00:13:13,910
Oh, Kiku!

167
00:13:16,710 --> 00:13:18,570
You betrayed me!

168
00:13:19,250 --> 00:13:21,710
And brought me shame!

169
00:13:23,410 --> 00:13:24,240
Ah!

170
00:13:24,323 --> 00:13:25,790
Why did I do that in public?

171
00:13:27,590 --> 00:13:28,930
What was I thinking?

172
00:13:32,450 --> 00:13:34,890
He's become a demon of fury!

173
00:13:40,970 --> 00:13:41,800
Okiku!

174
00:13:42,950 --> 00:13:43,790
Oh no!

175
00:13:44,050 --> 00:13:45,250
I know that pose!

176
00:13:45,490 --> 00:13:46,961
That's the far-bang slap!

177
00:13:47,050 --> 00:13:48,727
It sends you straight to hell!

178
00:13:48,810 --> 00:13:50,067
Can't we talk this through?

179
00:13:50,150 --> 00:13:51,750
Let's not be hasty.

180
00:13:57,790 --> 00:13:58,990
A shame.

181
00:14:02,370 --> 00:14:06,830
In the end, you are the kind of
beast who would strike a woman.

182
00:14:11,530 --> 00:14:13,770
And I shall strike you dead!

183
00:14:30,030 --> 00:14:32,150
Now come, come!

184
00:14:34,150 --> 00:14:35,890
You won't slip!

185
00:15:31,490 --> 00:15:33,090
You rat!

186
00:15:34,510 --> 00:15:37,590
How in blazes did you counter my attack?

187
00:15:40,050 --> 00:15:43,970
And for that matter,
how do you know Okikupe?

188
00:15:45,790 --> 00:15:47,430
Get away!

189
00:15:48,870 --> 00:15:52,667
I have to tear Okiku
apart with my bare hands.

190
00:15:52,750 --> 00:15:55,587
Or my reputation will be ruined.

191
00:15:55,670 --> 00:15:58,527
Alright, I get it.

192
00:15:58,610 --> 00:16:00,707
Let me stretch.

193
00:16:00,790 --> 00:16:02,347
Let's

194
00:16:02,430 --> 00:16:09,430
see

195
00:16:10,690 --> 00:16:11,520
you

196
00:16:11,603 --> 00:16:12,433
get through me!

197
00:16:13,970 --> 00:16:14,800
Huh?

198
00:16:15,130 --> 00:16:16,210
Scared?

199
00:16:17,810 --> 00:16:20,910
I've never lost a sumo match!

200
00:16:24,970 --> 00:16:26,550
I said move!

201
00:16:26,930 --> 00:16:28,930
I'll crush you!

202
00:16:29,530 --> 00:16:31,150
But he said for slap!

203
00:16:45,930 --> 00:16:48,283
He's dodging every one of those attacks!

204
00:16:48,490 --> 00:16:50,170
This is really fast!

205
00:16:51,550 --> 00:16:52,710
Keep it up, brat!

206
00:16:53,410 --> 00:16:55,881
But you can't win if you don't fight back!

207
00:17:06,950 --> 00:17:08,150
Ear splitter!

208
00:17:11,690 --> 00:17:12,890
Eye splitter!

209
00:17:18,150 --> 00:17:19,470
Hold on!

210
00:17:19,750 --> 00:17:22,450
Pretty sure that's not legal, you cheater!

211
00:17:22,750 --> 00:17:24,110
I don't care!

212
00:17:25,950 --> 00:17:27,627
I am...

213
00:17:27,710 --> 00:17:29,770
A Yokozuna!

214
00:17:36,130 --> 00:17:37,010
Fine.

215
00:17:37,290 --> 00:17:38,370
No rules.

216
00:17:42,070 --> 00:17:43,227
Hold him, sir!

217
00:17:43,310 --> 00:17:44,369
we have a problem.

218
00:17:44,850 --> 00:17:45,680
Huh?

219
00:17:46,090 --> 00:17:49,266
The Yokozuna got his topknot
chopped off by some lady?

220
00:17:49,570 --> 00:17:50,864
He might start a riot.

221
00:17:51,070 --> 00:17:54,147
He tried to take revenge, and
now he's fighting some guy.

222
00:17:54,230 --> 00:17:55,610
Uh, who cares?

223
00:17:55,870 --> 00:17:58,164
And what do you want me to do about it?

224
00:18:04,470 --> 00:18:06,730
I don't have time for sumo.

225
00:18:06,930 --> 00:18:09,871
I'm too busy tearing this
little girl's cheek off.

226
00:18:13,310 --> 00:18:14,810
Have mercy on me!

227
00:18:15,050 --> 00:18:16,910
You can have your booboon back!

228
00:18:17,190 --> 00:18:19,230
Just don't pinch me!

229
00:18:22,190 --> 00:18:24,427
Oh, you're getting pinched, kid.

230
00:18:24,510 --> 00:18:25,810
Sorry about it.

231
00:18:26,110 --> 00:18:29,522
You shouldn't have gone around
mentioning the Kozuki clan.

232
00:18:33,610 --> 00:18:37,910
The Kozuki clan is gonna come
back, and then you'll die!

233
00:18:40,210 --> 00:18:45,730
Even a dumb brat like you knows that uttering
the name Kozuki is a serious offense.

234
00:18:47,110 --> 00:18:49,050
You won't get off easy.

235
00:18:50,150 --> 00:18:53,915
You should have agreed to work
with us while you had the chance.

236
00:18:56,350 --> 00:18:57,970
It's been long enough.

237
00:18:58,230 --> 00:18:59,990
Stop chasing after ghosts.

238
00:19:00,330 --> 00:19:03,250
There hasn't been a
Kozuki here in 20 years.

239
00:19:04,070 --> 00:19:07,950
We shut them down after they
tried to destroy the land of Wano.

240
00:19:08,270 --> 00:19:10,890
They're nothing but evil spirits now

241
00:19:31,530 --> 00:19:32,910
Scram, you pest!

242
00:19:34,070 --> 00:19:38,710
And Okiku, you dug your own
grave, you little ingrate, eh?

243
00:19:40,430 --> 00:19:44,807
You have no right to turn down a request
from a member of the warrior class,

244
00:19:44,890 --> 00:19:45,720
you peasant.

245
00:19:47,170 --> 00:19:48,710
You shamed me.

246
00:19:49,890 --> 00:19:53,070
My honor demands that
I smash your head in.

247
00:20:08,170 --> 00:20:09,817
Then it's no problem, right?

248
00:20:10,050 --> 00:20:12,579
Go ahead and smash me
if you think you can.

249
00:20:25,810 --> 00:20:28,830
That should be easy for
a champ like you, right?

250
00:20:30,970 --> 00:20:32,750
You mock me?

251
00:20:34,230 --> 00:20:35,060
Listen!

252
00:20:36,730 --> 00:20:38,850
You know who I am!

253
00:20:39,350 --> 00:20:43,510
I'm the greatest Yokozuna in all Wano!

254
00:20:47,430 --> 00:20:49,170
All banks slip!

255
00:21:06,290 --> 00:21:08,050
What the heck is that?

256
00:21:08,350 --> 00:21:09,930
A rope, maybe?

257
00:21:24,910 --> 00:21:31,290
True, you may be a Yokozuna, but me?

258
00:21:35,710 --> 00:21:39,210
I'm the man who's going to
be the king of the pirates!

259
00:21:44,950 --> 00:21:46,990
I'm so scared!

260
00:21:47,390 --> 00:21:49,910
Please help me love me!

261
00:21:51,470 --> 00:21:53,070
Now come, come!

262
00:22:10,210 --> 00:22:11,040
Huh?

263
00:22:15,870 --> 00:22:17,270
GIANT!

264
00:22:20,210 --> 00:22:21,490
You won't fly!

265
00:22:43,650 --> 00:22:46,450
Toss Conney!

266
00:23:07,190 --> 00:23:09,230
Don't mention me!

267
00:23:16,930 --> 00:23:18,330
Whoa!

268
00:23:19,670 --> 00:23:20,750
Whoa!

269
00:23:52,710 --> 00:23:55,270
Saul, am I safe now, or what?

270
00:24:07,650 --> 00:24:10,310
The Yokozuna is out!

271
00:24:10,610 --> 00:24:13,930
I don't even know where he is!

272
00:24:15,510 --> 00:24:17,490
He really lost!

273
00:24:17,990 --> 00:24:21,166
After all those fights he
lost to that odd little guy?

274
00:24:31,130 --> 00:24:33,530
Now I'm a Yokozuna too!

275
00:24:34,490 --> 00:24:37,830
If anybody else wants to
fight, then bring it on!

276
00:24:41,650 --> 00:24:43,207
I think that'll do it.

277
00:24:43,290 --> 00:24:45,330
The boss is bound to show up.

278
00:24:45,950 --> 00:24:47,070
Ain't better!

279
00:24:48,070 --> 00:24:49,670
I know that guy!

280
00:24:50,250 --> 00:24:51,080
Wait!

281
00:24:51,163 --> 00:24:51,993
I know him too!

282
00:24:52,076 --> 00:24:54,068
He killed the magistrate, didn't he?

283
00:25:06,910 --> 00:25:08,790
You wanna fight about it?

284
00:25:15,230 --> 00:25:17,950
Don't tell me he's allies with that sumo!

285
00:25:22,650 --> 00:25:23,480
Hey!

286
00:25:24,990 --> 00:25:27,510
We want to fight the boss of this town!

287
00:25:51,310 --> 00:25:53,790
Tell them we're here to save Tama!
